<p>Ukraine’s armed forces shot down more than 33,000 Russian drones of various types in March, Defence Minister Mykhailo Fedorov said, describing it as the highest monthly figure since Russia launched its full-scale invasion. The reports said Ukraine used interceptor systems and is scaling up drone defences as Russian aerial attacks continue. Ukraine also says it uses long-range drones against targets inside Russia, including oil installations that provide revenue for Moscow’s war effort.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/4Bm2tQunIyhQhvQl3OGH3P1jcBUcGTSjbpm3q9Mn9_6U_hnJucB7GsmT9welPXSRtxbY1pzybki0zgvJYBKxKpVXdu-CksdNKqZJcedi8C6hawpDtZTkvvR4XdYh988bFDJwvQfJhEJu1cViqDVUU8wwACYBt37L-vFhvJVDFaWwEkb_oGYzYcer87eACbDmE2mf1WLn3BVMKbaK8HvfwtWCz6HpDbdfjij151V3k3E5Kij_TRhdc-t94ErJ-qoJM1XKF4hrlRy5ZF1SDA' alt='Police officers inspect fragments of a Russian drone after an air attack in Kyiv on Tuesday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Battlefield role: Ukrainian officials have described Ukraine’s drone technology as essential to slowing Russia’s larger army.</li><li>Energy targets: Ukraine’s Defence Ministry said longer-range drones have allowed strikes on Russian oil installations that provide revenue for Moscow’s war effort.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Ukrainian Defence Ministry: The ministry said Ukraine can now hit targets roughly 1,750 kilometers behind enemy lines, compared with about 630 kilometers at the start of Russia’s full-scale invasion. (<a href='https://www.clickondetroit.com/news/world/2026/04/28/ukraine-says-it-shot-down-33000-russian-drones-in-march-a-monthly-record/'>ClickOnDetroit</a>)</li><li>Mykhailo Fedorov: The defence minister said on Telegram that Ukraine is increasing interceptor-drone supplies and has set up a new air-force command to strengthen aerial defence. (<a href='https://www.nocutnews.co.kr/news/6510002'>NoCutNews</a>)</li><li>Russian authorities: After Ukrainian drones hit a Black Sea refinery and terminal, Russian officials evacuated local residents and warned of possible environmental consequences. (<a href='https://www.clickondetroit.com/news/world/2026/04/28/ukraine-says-it-shot-down-33000-russian-drones-in-march-a-monthly-record/'>ClickOnDetroit</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/russia-central-asia/article/3351755/ukraine-shot-down-33000-russian-drones-1-month-defence-minister'>Ukraine shot down 33,000 Russian drones in 1 month: defence minister</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-ukraine-russian-war-drones-putin-zelensky/'>Ukraine shot down 33,000 Russian drones in March, a monthly record, defence minister says</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cvgzd4qk7qgo'>Ukraine reports intercepting more than 33,000 Russian drones in March, the highest monthly total since the start of the full-scale invasion.</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/my-europe/2026/04/28/ukraine-says-it-shot-down-33000-russian-drones-in-march-a-new-monthly-record'>Ukraine says it shot down 33,000 Russian drones in March, a new monthly record</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.clickondetroit.com/news/world/2026/04/28/ukraine-says-it-shot-down-33000-russian-drones-in-march-a-monthly-record/'>Ukraine says it shot down 33,000 Russian drones in March, a monthly record</a> - clickondetroit.com</li><li><a href='https://www.military.com/daily-news/2026/04/28/ukraine-says-it-shot-down-33000-russian-drones-march-monthly-record.html'>Ukraine Says It Shot Down 33,000 Russian Drones in March, a Monthly Record</a> - military.com</li><li><a href='https://n1info.rs/svet/ukrajina-oborila-vise-od-33000-dronova-u-martu-sto-je-mesecni-rekord-od-pocetka-rata/'>Ukrajina oborila više od 33.000 dronova u martu, što je mesečni rekord od početka rata</a> - n1info.rs</li><li><a href='https://www.index.hr/vijesti/clanak/ukrajina-u-ozujku-smo-oborili-rekordan-broj-ruskih-dronova/278